{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>Come</b> — One says to another: לכו בואו (come, come), like לכו נא ונוכחה (come now and let us reason). And the meaning: come to us." "<b>Awesome</b> — Joined with מעשה (deed): awesome [is] the deed. And one who says that the heh is superfluous and it is like עליון, he strays, for the heh is a feminine marker, for a superfluous heh is not found in nouns unless the word is mil'ra and has a shureq and shureqa, like צדק and צדקה."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 66, :notes {1 "The argument is compressed: he addresses why the feminine form נורא appears. His examples צדק/צדקה and reference to mil'ra with shureq are terse; translated hyper-literally without expanding the grammatical point."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:32:54.339995984Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}